 "edits": [
  {
   "op": "replace_brief",
   "brief": "pc-maoi",
   "html": "<div class=\"brief sp pc\" id=\"pc-maoi\" data-entry=\"card\" data-lens=\"psych\" data-spine=\"2\" data-shelf=\"psych\" data-bp=\"behav\" data-nid=\"1477433010779 1477433015124 1477432963694 1485048836271 1485048840582 1485048831798 1485048880722 1519868339988 1485048874704 1506031358005 1485048818628 1485048822971 1485048795602 1485048768062 1485047130408 1485048774787 1484792776717\">\n<p class=\"pc-grp\">01 Antidepressants <span>&middot;</span> class card</p>\n<h4>MAOIs</h4>\n<p class=\"sub\">monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs) &middot; phenelzine &middot; tranylcypromine &middot; isocarboxazid &middot; selegiline patch</p>\n<div class=\"dp\"><span class=\"lbl\">Key point</span><ul class=\"bl\">\n<li><b>Tyramine</b> (aged cheese, wine) or a <b>sympathomimetic</b> such as pseudoephedrine on an MAOI <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>hypertensive crisis</b>; treat with <b>phentolamine</b></li>\n<li>Any other <b>serotonergic drug</b> with an MAOI <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>serotonin syndrome</b>; wait <b>2 weeks</b> between them, <b>5 weeks</b> after <b>fluoxetine</b></li>\n<li><b>Not first line</b>; used for treatment-resistant or <b>atypical</b> depression; <b>lethal in overdose</b></li>\n</ul></div>\n<div class=\"sp-script sp-s2 pc-script\"><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Drugs</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b>Phenelzine</b> <span class=\"pc-tn\">Nardil</span></p><p><b>Tranylcypromine</b> <span class=\"pc-tn\">Parnate</span></p><p><b>Isocarboxazid</b> <span class=\"pc-tn\">Marplan</span></p><p><b>Selegiline</b> patch <span class=\"pc-tn\">Emsam</span>: selective for MAO‑B at low doses</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Mechanism</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b>Monoamine oxidase (MAO) A and B</b> blocked, irreversibly <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> less breakdown of serotonin, norepinephrine and dopamine <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-1\">A and B</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-1\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">The two enzymes</span>MAO‑A breaks down serotonin, norepinephrine and dopamine. MAO‑B breaks down dopamine. Phenelzine, tranylcypromine and isocarboxazid block both; selegiline at low doses and rasagiline block MAO‑B selectively.</span></p><p>Gut <b>MAO‑A</b> blocked <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> dietary <b>tyramine</b> enters the circulation <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> norepinephrine pushed out of nerve endings <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> <b>hypertensive crisis</b></p><p>Irreversible block <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> new enzyme must be made <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> diet limits and washout outlast the last dose (timeline below)</p><p><b>Selegiline</b>: MAO‑B only at low doses <span class=\"op op-a\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"leads to\"></span> gut MAO‑A spared at the low-dose patch</p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Uses</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b>Treatment-resistant</b> depression, <b>atypical</b> depression, anxiety; <b>not first line</b> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-2\">Why reserved</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-2\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Why MAOIs are reserved</span>Kept for severe, treatment-resistant depression because of the hypertensive crisis and their lethality in overdose. Tranylcypromine often works after several failed antidepressant trials.</span></p><p><b>Atypical features</b> (mood brightens with good news, more sleep and appetite, leaden paralysis): other first-line drugs first, an MAOI if they fail <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"mdd\">Major Depressive Disorder</button></p><p><b>Selegiline</b>: also <b>Parkinson disease</b>, as an MAO‑B inhibitor added when levodopa starts to wear off; may worsen levodopa adverse effects <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"parkinson\">Parkinson Disease and Parkinsonism</button></p></div></div><div class=\"sr\"><span class=\"sk\">Adverse effects</span><div class=\"sv\"><p><b>Hypertensive crisis</b> and <b>serotonin syndrome</b>: the two blocks below</p><p><b>Lethal in overdose</b> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"toxidrome\">Suspected Overdose or Toxidrome</button></p><p>Common: erectile dysfunction, <b>insomnia</b> and anxiety (central nervous system stimulation), dizziness, nausea, pedal edema, weight gain <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-3\">Timing</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-3\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Dose timing</span>Doses go in the morning and early afternoon to avoid overstimulation. Erectile dysfunction is least common with tranylcypromine.</span></p><p><b>Withdrawal</b> after an abrupt stop: vivid nightmares, agitation, psychosis, seizures; timing below</p><p>Orthostatic (postural) hypotension</p></div></div></div>\n<div class=\"sp-rows pc-blocks\">\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Tyramine crisis</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Severe hypertension, occipital headache, blurry vision and sweating within minutes of aged cheese, aged meats, wine or malted beer, or a decongestant such as pseudoephedrine</b><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> a hypertensive crisis follows tyramine on an MAOI, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">phentolamine, an alpha blocker that dilates vessels</span>. <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-4\">Not these</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-4\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Other antidotes offered</span>Cyproheptadine treats serotonin syndrome. Physostigmine treats severe anticholinergic toxicity, with hot, dry skin.</span></p><p class=\"pc-note\">Headache, a fast or slow pulse, or chest pain on an MAOI may mean a rise in blood pressure; intracranial bleeding has been reported</p></div>\n<div class=\"sp-row\"><span class=\"sp-src\">Serotonin syndrome</span><b class=\"sp-f\">Fever, mental status changes, autonomic instability, hyperreflexia and clonus after a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI), serotonin-norepinephrine reuptake inhibitor (SNRI), tricyclic, meperidine, tramadol, dextromethorphan, linezolid or St. John's wort</b><div class=\"sp-chips\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"ssri-effects\">SSRI Adverse Effects</button></div><p class=\"sp-commit\"><b>If</b> serotonin syndrome appears, <b>choose</b> <span class=\"mask\">stopping every serotonergic drug</span>.</p></div>\n</div>\n<figure class=\"lcw pc-lcw\"><div class=\"ttl\"><span>Toxicity and withdrawal, from the exposure or the last dose</span><small>not to scale</small></div><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Tyramine crisis</b><span class=\"win\">Within minutes of the trigger</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:12%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:23%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:55%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:89%\"></i><i class=\"bar c3\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:5%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:12%\">6 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:23%\">12 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:36%\">24 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:55%\">48 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:72%\">72 h</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:89%\">96 h</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Shows</b>severe hypertension, occipital headache, blurry vision, sweating</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Serotonin syndrome</b><span class=\"win\">Usually within 6 hours of a drug being added; nearly always within 24 hours</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:12%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:23%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:55%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:89%\"></i><i class=\"bar c3\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:12%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:12%\">6 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:23%\">12 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:36%\">24 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:55%\">48 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:72%\">72 h</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:89%\">96 h</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Shows</b>fever, mental status changes, autonomic instability, hyperreflexia, clonus</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Overdose</b><span class=\"win\">Few signs for the first 12 hours; worst at 24 to 48 hours <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-5\">Label</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-5\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Phenelzine label</span>On the Nardil label, signs can be absent or slight for the first 12 hours and then build slowly to a peak at 24 to 48 hours; deaths are reported, so the patient is admitted at once and watched continuously.</span></span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:12%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:23%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:55%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:89%\"></i><i class=\"bar c2\" style=\"--a:23%;--b:55%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:12%\">6 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:23%\">12 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:36%\">24 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:55%\">48 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:72%\">72 h</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:89%\">96 h</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Shows</b>lethal; admit and monitor through the whole window, even if the patient looks well early</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm mask\">Withdrawal after an abrupt stop</b><span class=\"win\">Usually 24 to 72 hours after the last dose</span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:12%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:23%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:36%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:55%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:72%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:89%\"></i><i class=\"bar c1\" style=\"--a:36%;--b:72%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:12%\">6 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:23%\">12 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:36%\">24 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:55%\">48 h</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:72%\">72 h</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:89%\">96 h</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Shows</b>vivid nightmares, agitation, psychosis, seizures</p></div></li></ol></figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx pc-tbl\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Interactions, by result</caption><thead><tr><th>Combined with</th><th>Result</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>SSRIs, SNRIs, tricyclics, St. John's wort</td><td><span>Serotonin syndrome</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Never together; washout below</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Meperidine, tramadol, dextromethorphan</td><td><span>Serotonin syndrome</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Avoid</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Linezolid, a weak MAOI</td><td><span>Serotonin syndrome</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Avoid</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Pseudoephedrine, other sympathomimetics</td><td><span>Hypertensive crisis</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Avoid</span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Aged or overripe foods, malted beer, certain wines <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-6\">Foods</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-6\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">Tyramine and dopamine foods</span>Aged cheese, aged meats, malted beers, Chianti, sherry, liqueurs, and overripe or aged foods such as fava beans, yeast extracts, soy sauce.</span></td><td><span>Hypertensive crisis</span></td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Avoid these foods every day</span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure class=\"lcw pc-lcw\"><div class=\"ttl\"><span>Washout and diet limits, from the last dose</span><small>weeks</small></div><ol class=\"wrows\"><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm\">MAOI, then a serotonergic drug</b><span class=\"win\"><span class=\"mask\">2 weeks</span></span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:15%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:30%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:45%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:60%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:75%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c2\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:30%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:15%\">1 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:30%\">2 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:45%\">3 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:60%\">4 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:75%\">5 wk</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:90%\">6 wk</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Why</b>the block is irreversible; the enzyme has to be made again</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm\">Another antidepressant, then an MAOI</b><span class=\"win\"><span class=\"mask\">2 weeks</span></span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:15%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:30%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:45%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:60%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:75%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c2\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:30%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:15%\">1 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:30%\">2 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:45%\">3 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:60%\">4 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:75%\">5 wk</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:90%\">6 wk</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Why</b>serotonin syndrome if they overlap</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm\">Fluoxetine, then an MAOI</b><span class=\"win\"><span class=\"mask\">5 weeks</span></span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:15%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:30%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:45%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:60%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:75%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c3\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:75%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:15%\">1 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:30%\">2 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:45%\">3 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:60%\">4 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:75%\">5 wk</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:90%\">6 wk</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Why</b>long half-life</p></div></li><li class=\"wr\"><div class=\"wh\"><b class=\"nm\">Diet limits after the last MAOI dose</b><span class=\"win\"><span class=\"mask\">2 weeks</span> <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-pop\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"pcm-pop-7\">In practice</button><span class=\"sp-pop-b\" id=\"pcm-pop-7\" hidden><span class=\"sp-ct\">In practice</span>StatPearls advises keeping the diet for 4 weeks after the last dose, longer than the Step 2 window.</span></span></div><div class=\"wb\"><div class=\"rail\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:0%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:15%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:30%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:45%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:60%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:75%\"></i><i class=\"tk\" style=\"--x:90%\"></i><i class=\"bar c1\" style=\"--a:0%;--b:30%\"></i></div><div class=\"rax\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"a0\" style=\"--x:0%\">0</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:15%\">1 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:30%\">2 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:45%\">3 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:60%\">4 wk</span><span class=\"\" style=\"--x:75%\">5 wk</span><span class=\"a1\" style=\"--x:90%\">6 wk</span><em>&rarr;</em></div><p class=\"wl\"><b>Why</b>tyramine crisis until the enzyme returns</p></div></li></ol></figure>\n<div class=\"sp-dx pc-tbl\"><table class=\"dense\"><caption>Monitoring and limits</caption><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>Check</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Every day on an MAOI</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Tyramine diet; no decongestants or serotonergic drugs</span></span></td><td><span>Hypertensive crisis; serotonin syndrome</span></td></tr><tr><td>Selegiline patch, low dose</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">No specific diet limits</span></span></td><td><span>MAO‑B only at low doses</span></td></tr><tr><td>Stopping an MAOI</td><td><span><span class=\"mask\">Diet limits continue; washout as in the timeline</span></span></td><td><span>The block is irreversible</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"pc-owners\"><span class=\"lbl\">Where the choice is made</span>\n<p>Whether to use an MAOI <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"mdd\">Major Depressive Disorder</button></p>\n<p>Selegiline as a levodopa adjunct <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"parkinson\">Parkinson Disease and Parkinsonism</button></p>\n<p>Managing serotonin syndrome <button type=\"button\" class=\"sp-drw\" data-brief=\"ssri-effects\">SSRI Adverse Effects</button></p>\n</div>\n\n<h5 class=\"authored-hdr\" id=\"pcm-bank\">Practice</h5>\n<ol class=\"bank authored\">\n<li data-type=\"next\" data-d1=\"Stop fluoxetine, wait 2 weeks, then start\" data-d2=\"Start now while tapering fluoxetine\" data-item-id=\"q_66f40af9d2cc8da1efea\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_60b7fe3b7fb3e799bdd8\" data-d1-id=\"o_7e409434420531afcca8\" data-d2-id=\"o_056584f8c36aa3d0e866\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\" data-key-why=\"Fluoxetine has a long half-life: 5 weeks before an MAOI\" data-d1-why=\"Two weeks suits other serotonergic drugs, not fluoxetine\" data-d2-why=\"Overlap with an MAOI risks serotonin syndrome\"><span class=\"sl\">41-year-old man with depression unresponsive to four antidepressant trials</span>\n<span class=\"si\">now on fluoxetine; his psychiatrist plans tranylcypromine</span>\n<span class=\"si\">no psychotic features, no suicidal ideation</span>\n<span class=\"si\">asks when the new drug can start</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">BP 124/80 mm Hg &middot; HR 72/min</span> &rarr; <b>Stop fluoxetine, wait 5 weeks, then start</b> &rarr; fluoxetine has a long half-life, so 5 weeks must pass before an MAOI; at least 2 weeks must pass after other serotonergic drugs, and any overlap risks serotonin syndrome</li>\n<li data-type=\"next\" data-d1=\"Cyproheptadine\" data-d2=\"Physostigmine\" data-item-id=\"q_be52a4a6b9ef46ca4b78\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_3de573dae1f1c4112f73\" data-d1-id=\"o_164d804d530fd7d8de3c\" data-d2-id=\"o_ab16cc33d1f4f511edab\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?\" data-key-why=\"Tyramine on an MAOI: hypertensive crisis; phentolamine, an alpha blocker\" data-d1-why=\"Cyproheptadine is for serotonin syndrome: a serotonergic drug and clonus\" data-d2-why=\"Physostigmine reverses anticholinergic toxicity: dry skin, not sweating\"><span class=\"sl\">48-year-old woman on phenelzine at a wine-and-cheese party</span>\n<span class=\"si\">sudden blurred vision and drenching sweat</span>\n<span class=\"si\">no new medicines; no tremor or clonus</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">BP 228/124 mm Hg &middot; HR 112/min &middot; T 37.1 °C</span> &rarr; <b>Phentolamine</b> &rarr; wine and aged cheese on an MAOI bring a tyramine hypertensive crisis, treated with phentolamine; cyproheptadine is for serotonin syndrome, and physostigmine for severe anticholinergic toxicity with hot, dry skin</li>\n<li data-type=\"dx\" data-d1=\"Tyramine hypertensive crisis\" data-d2=\"Anticholinergic toxicity\" data-item-id=\"q_70916c313e18fb99ed19\" data-item-version=\"1\" data-item-status=\"ready\" data-key-id=\"o_10d121e4d70d11b1b695\" data-d1-id=\"o_71bfde05d6cbd9323d9d\" data-d2-id=\"o_e19cf5eef0d9e1a45eed\" data-src=\"authored\" data-lead-in=\"Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\" data-key-why=\"MAOI plus meperidine: fever, hyperreflexia, clonus\" data-d1-why=\"Follows aged food or a sympathomimetic, not an opioid\" data-d2-why=\"Hot, dry skin; this patient sweats\"><span class=\"sl\">56-year-old man on phenelzine given meperidine after knee surgery</span>\n<span class=\"si\">3 hours later agitated, sweating and shivering</span>\n<span class=\"si\">hyperreflexia; clonus at both ankles</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">T 39.4 °C &middot; BP 168/96 mm Hg &middot; HR 124/min</span> &rarr; <b>Serotonin syndrome</b> &rarr; meperidine is contraindicated with an MAOI because the pair causes serotonin syndrome, typically fever, autonomic instability, hyperreflexia and clonus; the tyramine crisis follows aged food or a sympathomimetic, and anticholinergic toxicity leaves the skin dry</li>\n</ol>\n</div>",
   "ledger": "repair/migration/pharm/MAOI/spine/claim_map.json",
   "note": "decision spine v2: pc-maoi"
  }
 ]
}